WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.362
The federal requirement, from
the guide's requirements table.

2
00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:08.652
Gate five supports R A five, vulnerability
monitoring and scanning, S I two,

3
00:00:08.652 --> 00:00:13.161
flaw remediation, and C M eight,
the system component inventory,

4
00:00:13.161 --> 00:00:18.624
all from NIST special publication eight
hundred fifty-three, revision five.

5
00:00:18.624 --> 00:00:23.075
The evidence is the vulnerability
query output and the remediation queue.

6
00:00:23.075 --> 00:00:28.574
Gate six supports the incident response
family: I R four, incident handling;

7
00:00:28.574 --> 00:00:32.920
I R five, incident monitoring;
and I R six, incident reporting;

8
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:37.000
with A U six, audit record
review, analysis and reporting.

9
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.987
The evidence is the incident
exports, with their classification.

10
00:00:40.987 --> 00:00:45.093
Each row lines up with fed-ramp
twenty X key security indicators,

11
00:00:45.093 --> 00:00:50.362
which bind cloud service providers; the
agency lines its own evidence up with them.

12
00:00:50.362 --> 00:00:52.452
The gates support these controls,

13
00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:55.730
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.
